1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

8
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

9
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:22,917
Don’t be shy!

10
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Sing out loud!

12
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

13
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,167
Let your imagination shine!

14
00:00:30,417 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

15
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

16
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:34,000
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
ODEER MAYO / Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan

18
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
Pulling Radishes in the Countryside

19
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,333
May’s family is visiting the countryside together today.

20
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:47,417
Dad drove for a long time.

21
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,167
At last, they arrived at Grandpa and Grandma’s house.

22
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:52,833
Grandpa! Grandma!

23
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:55,167
Well, look at that! May and Little Deer, you’re finally here!

24
00:00:55,167 --> 00:00:57,417
Grandma, look! Look!

25
00:00:57,417 --> 00:00:58,833
I’ve already put on my little rain boots.

26
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:00,167
Let’s hurry and go!

27
00:01:00,167 --> 00:01:01,917
L-let’s go!

28
00:01:01,917 --> 00:01:03,917
Not so fast. Let’s take precautions first

29
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,917
so you don’t get covered in mosquito bites.

30
00:01:05,917 --> 00:01:09,583
Grandma sprayed mosquito repellent on May and everyone else.

31
00:01:10,417 --> 00:01:12,000
I want to go, too!

32
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:12,667
No slacking off!

33
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:15,667
Getting exercise in the countryside is good for your health.

34
00:01:15,667 --> 00:01:16,833
Let’s go!

35
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:20,667
We’ll cook a big feast while you’re gone!

36
00:01:21,083 --> 00:01:24,667
May’s family walked into the vegetable garden together.

37
00:01:26,917 --> 00:01:28,583
That flower is huge!

38
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:32,167
I could sit inside and be a flower fairy!

39
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:33,583
Hehehe, May!

40
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:35,833
That’s not a flower. It’s a cabbage!

41
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:36,833
It’s very fresh.

42
00:01:36,833 --> 00:01:40,083
What? So this is the cabbage I love to eat!

43
00:01:40,917 --> 00:01:43,333
Little Deer, you can’t eat it like that!

44
00:01:43,333 --> 00:01:45,583
Little Deer wants to eat everything.

45
00:01:45,583 --> 00:01:47,167
Haha!

46
00:01:48,083 --> 00:01:50,417
We already harvested the cabbages this morning.

47
00:01:50,417 --> 00:01:52,583
Today, we need help over here.

48
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,083
The radish field!

49
00:01:55,583 --> 00:01:57,583
Grandpa, where are the radishes?

50
00:01:57,583 --> 00:01:58,833
I can’t see any.

51
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:01,667
May, the radishes are still hiding underground.

52
00:02:01,667 --> 00:02:05,667
If their leaves flower, the radishes won’t taste as good.

53
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:08,667
So we need to harvest them now.

54
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:10,750
Radishes can be prickly, so remember to wear gloves.

55
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:14,583
First, hold the top of the radish.

56
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:20,917
Loosen the soil, then grab its stem.

57
00:02:30,583 --> 00:02:30,917
Mm-hmm.

58
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:35,000
Ah!

59
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,250
Hahaha! What a tiny one!

60
00:02:37,833 --> 00:02:39,667
That looks easy. I’ll try, too!

61
00:02:40,167 --> 00:02:40,667
Heave-ho!

62
00:02:41,167 --> 00:02:41,667
Heave-ho!

63
00:02:48,833 --> 00:02:50,250
Hehe, Little Deer.

64
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:52,833
You need to grab the stem lower down.

65
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:55,000
Like this.

66
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,917
Mm-hmm.

67
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,083
Wow! Little Deer is naturally strong!

68
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:07,417
All right! I’ll succeed, too!

69
00:03:09,583 --> 00:03:13,250
I need to be as strong as an elephant!

70
00:03:13,583 --> 00:03:16,167
Uh…

71
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:21,333
Why won’t it move?

72
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:23,000
Could there be…

73
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,833
a little fairy playing tug-of-war with me down there?

74
00:03:26,583 --> 00:03:29,083
May, do you need help?

75
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,833
Nope! I have a secret trick!

76
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:32,167
Pull, pull, pull!

77
00:03:32,417 --> 00:03:33,583
Pull, pull, pull!

78
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:36,917
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

79
00:03:37,417 --> 00:03:38,583
I can’t pull it out!

80
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:40,833
Pull the radish, pull the radish!

81
00:03:40,833 --> 00:03:42,250
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

82
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:43,667
I can’t pull it out!

83
00:03:43,667 --> 00:03:45,167
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

84
00:03:46,250 --> 00:03:46,667
Come on!

85
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:47,333
Come on!

86
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:53,833
Grandpa, look! It’s a giant radish!

87
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,500
It was just feeling shy!

88
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:55,833
Haha! Hooray!

89
00:03:56,167 --> 00:03:58,083
Haha! Great!

90
00:03:58,083 --> 00:04:01,500
Life in the countryside isn’t easy. Farmers work so hard!

91
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,917
That’s right. We should respect our food.

92
00:04:03,917 --> 00:04:06,417
The fallen leaves can be fed to the chickens, too.

93
00:04:06,417 --> 00:04:08,417
That’s the cycle of nature.

94
00:04:08,417 --> 00:04:10,667
All right, let’s keep pulling radishes!

95
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,500
May and Little Deer sang as they pulled radishes.

96
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:16,417
Grandpa’s bamboo basket was full in no time.

97
00:04:16,417 --> 00:04:18,583
There’s just one radish left. Who wants to pull it?

98
00:04:18,583 --> 00:04:20,333
Me! Me! Me!

99
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:24,833
This one is shy, too. Let’s figure out how to get it together.

100
00:04:24,833 --> 00:04:27,083
Little Deer, are you ready?

101
00:04:27,083 --> 00:04:28,583
Ready? Sing!

102
00:04:28,583 --> 00:04:32,917
Pull the radish, pull the radish! Heave-ho, heave-ho! Pull the radish!

103
00:04:32,917 --> 00:04:36,667
Heave-ho, heave-ho! It won’t budge!

104
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:38,667
I’m so tired! Why won’t it come out?

105
00:04:38,667 --> 00:04:41,417
Oh, this radish must be really big.

106
00:04:41,417 --> 00:04:43,500
Dad will help you pull it out.

107
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:46,917
Little Deer, May, and Dad all pulled together.

108
00:04:46,917 --> 00:04:50,667
Heave-ho, heave-ho, pull the radish! Heave-ho, heave-ho, pull the radish!

109
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:54,500
Pull the radish, pull the radish! Heave-ho, heave-ho!

110
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:57,250
This one really is a tough one!

111
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:58,667
Watch me!

112
00:04:58,667 --> 00:04:59,417
Hah!

113
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:07,250
Waaah!

114
00:05:07,417 --> 00:05:07,750
Waaah!

115
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:10,333
Goodness! I’ve never seen a radish this big!

116
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:13,500
This must be the shyest Radish King ever!

117
00:05:13,917 --> 00:05:16,750
Hahaha! That’s so cool!

118
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:21,333
The family returned home with a huge harvest to add to Grandma’s meal.

119
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:23,083
Wow, what a big radish!

120
00:05:23,083 --> 00:05:24,083
Grandma! Mom!

121
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:26,583
I pulled the biggest radish today!

122
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:28,750
Dad pulled the smallest one! Haha!

123
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:31,083
Oh my! You’re all amazing!

124
00:05:31,083 --> 00:05:32,583
You must be hungry.

125
00:05:32,583 --> 00:05:34,417
Lunch is ready!

126
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:39,167
I made stir-fried cabbage, turnip cakes, radish pancakes, and radish soup.

127
00:05:39,167 --> 00:05:41,500
Wow! A radish feast!

128
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:41,833
Mmm, delicious!

129
00:05:43,667 --> 00:05:44,000
Mmm, delicious!

130
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,500
Grandma, I have a secret for pulling radishes!

131
00:05:47,583 --> 00:05:51,083
You pull the radishes while singing the radish-pulling song!

132
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:57,917
Heave-ho, pull! Heave-ho, pull!
